# Health > Disk: the storage folders whose biggest subfolders the page lists.
#
# Copy this file to <config>/project-dashboard/disk.conf and edit it
# (<config> is $SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/system). Folder paths
# describe a machine, so the real list stays outside the checkout. Without a
# disk.conf the Disk area still shows volume use and build output, and one
# unknown row names this file.
#
# One folder per line; ~ and $HOME expand:
#
#   storage|<path>
#
# Each folder costs one `du -k -d 1` inside the Disk area's 8 second budget.
# A folder du cannot finish in what is left is a row that says so; a folder
# that does not exist (an ejected volume) is one too. A line the page cannot
# read is named on the page and skipped.
storage|/Volumes/change-me/repo-storage
